# (black key 1: as a step key it would launch pattern A, so a step recorded is a note played)
# Recording on a WEFT track and on a PERC track with one machine, as on a synth track (v1.22.2): with REC
# armed on SEQ the keys play and record notes, not steps; stopped and armed, step recording takes them.
wait 300
kind 1 6
wait 100
expect tp 1 KIND 6
tap SEQ
wait 150
expect steps 1 0
tap PLAY
tap REC
wait 200
key 1 down
wait 120
key 1 up
wait 300
key 1 down
wait 120
key 1 up
wait 300
expect steps 1 2
tap REC
tap PLAY
wait 200
# stopped and armed, on an empty WEFT track: step recording
kind 3 6
turn ALGO 2
wait 100
tap REC
wait 100
expect sreccur 1
key 0 down
wait 50
key 0 up
wait 50
expect sreccur 2
expect stepnote 3 1 53
tap REC
wait 100
turn ALGO -2
wait 100
# a PERC track with one machine (not a kit)
kind 2 3
settp 2 MODE 0
wait 100
turn ALGO 1
wait 100
tap SEQ
wait 150
expect steps 2 0
tap PLAY
tap REC
wait 200
key 1 down
wait 120
key 1 up
wait 300
expect steps 2 1
tap REC
tap PLAY
